  "slug": "drug-sensitivity-20b3",
  "summary": "Reproducible omics workflows now span single-cell, spatial, and bulk data, increasingly with LLM or interactive interfaces.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is software that makes omics analysis run under explicit, reproducible structure. NNclinSSOAP implements a modular, GxP-ready Nextflow pipeline linking single-cell and Xenium spatial transcriptomics to annotated objects and tissue maps, while AstraKit provides an open-source KNIME suite spanning variant interpretation, multi-omics integration and drug-screen matching. BULLKpy and EMTscore extend this to bulk RNA-seq frameworks and EMT pathway gene set scoring. The set is heterogeneous, and not every item shares this structure. What is new is pairing such workflows with LLM-assisted or interactive interfaces: CytoAnalyst applies Llama prompting under ontology and marker constraints for cell type annotation, while Age effect explorer, MRDviz and SPAC provide Shiny or web front ends for browsing, simulation and single-cell spatial analysis.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
